yload on this the  red and the carbon fiber finish on this  looks so good you can obviously tell if  this is well equipped for a larger  camera because you have so much more  space  compared to this one so when you're kind  of deciding on which one you're gonna  get  it really does depend on first of all  what's your budget and what kind of  camera are you gonna be putting on this  thing  honestly for us i feel like most of the  time  this is kind of our setup but what i  like so much about this  is being able to fine tune your  adjustments so there's these little  knobs right here so as you can see when  you turn this knob  the plate moves and this will let you  get very very fine-tuned adjustments to  make sure you're getting the most stable  and perfectly even  so here they are let's take them out for  a test  [Music]  do you think i look cool i mean i'm  wearing two patterns of camo  and some really cool cheetah shoes  honestly i would be friends with myself  so this is the first time that we're  bringing them outside  and this one is definitely heavier i  really  love how light this is and i can just  easily  manipulate it and this one we actually  have hooked up to the raven eye  we have active track already set up this  will also send a signal to my phone  when i do have it connected to the raven  eye but it's cool because this is  actually a touch screen  that is another difference between the  two is the rs2 does have a touchscreen  and the other one does not  it has a very small display screen which  will still let you view settings  but you can't touch to control and then  here is the rsc2 i am going to be going  on a trip for the first time in seven  months  so i'm gonna take this one with me  because this one does fold down into a  really nice little storage  uh contraption i can't figure out the  words that i want to say  it folds down to be small this one  actually folds down to be pretty small  too  but i can't take both tyler  what if i take rsc2  y